__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Print artifacts are build output, not source. `printing/generate-all.sh`
# rebuilds every one of them from the markdown, and committing them cost
# a full new copy of each file per rebuild — a PDF is compressed binary,
# so git cannot store one as a small difference from the last one the way
# it does for prose. See printing/README.md.
printing/*.pdf

# The named-character sheet build. `generate-sheets.py` with no arguments
# makes the blank handout, which is tracked; naming characters makes this
# instead, which never has been. It is a filled copy of what is already in
# `campaign/`, so it is output rather than source, and it was landing in the
# tree untracked every time anybody ran the named build.
printing/character-sheets-filled.html
